@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction to Azure Artifacts";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how Azure Artifacts helps manage dependencies and package management in Azure DevOps.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- What is Azure Artifacts? -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What is Azure Artifacts?</h2>
        <p>
            Azure Artifacts is a package management solution integrated into Azure DevOps. It enables teams to create, host, and share packages using feeds. It supports various package formats, including NuGet, npm, Maven, Python, and Universal Packages.
        </p>
        <p>
            With Azure Artifacts, developers can maintain a centralized and secure repository for managing dependencies efficiently.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-artifacts-overview.jpg" alt="Azure Artifacts Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Artifacts simplifies package management across teams.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Benefits of Azure Artifacts -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Benefits of Using Azure Artifacts</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Secure Package Storage:</strong> Store and manage dependencies securely.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Integration with CI/CD:</strong> Seamlessly integrate with Azure Pipelines.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Multi-format Support:</strong> Supports NuGet, npm, Maven, and more.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Scoped Feeds:</strong> Manage multiple feeds with role-based access control.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Versioning Control:</strong> Maintain package versions and control updates.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/benefits-azure-artifacts.jpg" alt="Benefits of Azure Artifacts" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Artifacts streamlines dependency management.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- How to Use Azure Artifacts -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">How to Use Azure Artifacts</h2>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Go to Azure DevOps and navigate to the "Artifacts" section.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Create a new feed for hosting your packages.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Connect to the feed using CLI tools such as npm, NuGet, or Maven.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Publish packages using the respective package manager.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Use the packages in your build and release pipelines.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/how-to-use-azure-artifacts.jpg" alt="Using Azure Artifacts" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Step-by-step guide to using Azure Artifacts effectively.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Best Practices for Azure Artifacts</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Scoped Feeds:</strong> Separate feeds for development, testing, and production.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enable Retention Policies:</strong> Clean up old packages automatically.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Implement Access Control:</strong> Restrict access to sensitive packages.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automate Publishing:</strong> Use Azure Pipelines to automate package updates.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor Dependencies:</strong> Regularly update and audit package versions.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/best-practices-azure-artifacts.jpg" alt="Best Practices for Azure Artifacts" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following best practices enhances security and efficiency.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Azure Artifacts is a powerful package management solution within Azure DevOps, offering seamless integration with CI/CD pipelines and support for multiple package formats. By leveraging its features, teams can improve dependency management and streamline software development workflows.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/conclusion-azure-artifacts.jpg" alt="Azure Artifacts Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Artifacts simplifies package distribution and management.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>